{"name":"Persian Blinds","hex":"#e3e1cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blinds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of blind"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of blind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blinds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window blind","blocks":[{"text":"A window blind is a type of window covering. There are many different kinds of window blinds which use a variety of control systems. A typical window blind is made up of several long horizontal or vertical slats of various types of hard material, including wood, plastic or metal which are held together by cords that run through the blind slats. Vertical blinds run along a track system which can tilt open and closed and move side-to-side. Window blinds can be manoeuvred with either a manual or remote control by rotating them from an open position, with slats spaced out, to a closed position where slats overlap and block out most of the light. There are also several types of window coverings, called shades, that use a single piece of soft material instead of slats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Some_window_blinds.JPG/330px-Some_window_blinds.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_blind","wikidata":"Q321046"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Window_blind_stopper.jpg/500px-Window_blind_stopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Window_blind_stopper.jpg/1280px-Window_blind_stopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Window_blind_stopper.jpg/500px-Window_blind_stopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","